  "content": {
    "id": "p66-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p66-q6-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A child has two bags containing marbles.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "His blue bag contains three red marbles, and two green marbles.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "His yellow bag contains four red marbles, and one green marble.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The child picks a bag and takes out one marble. Given that he picks his blue bag 60% of the time, find the probability of the following.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p66-q6a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The marble is green.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{8}{25}$",
          "worked": "Let $G$ be the event that the marble is green. Add the probabilities of the blue-bag and yellow-bag cases.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(G)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac25+\\frac25\\times\\frac15\\\\P(G)&=\\frac6{25}+\\frac2{25}\\\\P(G)&=\\frac8{25}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q6b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The marble is red.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{17}{25}$",
          "worked": "Let $R$ be the event that the marble is red. Add the probabilities of the blue-bag and yellow-bag cases.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(R)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac35+\\frac25\\times\\frac45\\\\P(R)&=\\frac9{25}+\\frac8{25}\\\\P(R)&=\\frac{17}{25}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q6c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "He picked the blue bag, given the marble is green.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p66-q6c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac34",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p66-q6c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the probability of blue bag and green marble by the total probability of green.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $B$ be the event that he picks the blue bag, and $G$ the event that the marble is green. From part (a), $P(G)=\\frac8{25}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B\\cap G)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac25\\\\P(B\\cap G)&=\\frac6{25}\\\\P(B\\mid G)&=\\frac{P(B\\cap G)}{P(G)}\\\\P(B\\mid G)&=\\frac{6/25}{8/25}\\\\P(B\\mid G)&=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      }
    ]
  },
